# Paths whose NAME has a credential shape and which hold no secret, exempted one by one.
#
# Read by pablo-protocol's guards/credentials-guard.sh, which refuses a path matching `*.env`,
# `*.pem`, `*.key`, `*.p8`, `*.p12`, `*.enc`, `*.dev.vars`, `*-sa.json` or an SSH identity name
# whatever the file contains — because a path rule is the only rule that still works on a blob
# the content rules cannot read.
#
# **Deliberately empty, and that is the answer rather than an oversight.** No path in this
# repository has a credential-shaped name and an innocent content: the one tracked file matching
# the list, `apps/lexitar/records/roster.enc`, is a real encrypted artifact and is being removed
# rather than exempted. An entry here over something real would be strictly worse than no guard,
# because it reads as a decision somebody checked.
#
# The file exists so that answer is on the record and so the next path with an `.enc` name has an
# obvious home. A whole-line comment parses to nothing, so an empty file and this one behave
# identically — the difference is only to a reader. Content exemptions are the other file,
# `credentials-allow-content`, which says what it covers and why.
